{title: Dry Bones Rise}
{subtitle: Ezekiel 37:1–10}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse (instrumental)}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Gm] | ×2
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]The hand of [Bb]the Lord came [Gm]upon me in a vision
Set me [Dm]down in a valley full of bones, [Bb]no living
[Gm]Very ma[Dm]ny, [Dm]very dry, [Bb]sun bleached, for[Gm]gotten
He said, son of man, can these [Dm]bones live again
I said, Lord, you [Bb]know, I can't [Gm]answer that
[Dm]He [Gm]said, prophe[Dm]sy to the bones, tell them this is [Bb]a fact
Hear the word of the [Gm]Lord, I will [Dm]breathe into you
Put flesh on your frame and you will live, it's true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Dry bones rise, dry bones rise
Hear the word of the Lord tonight
Breath from the four winds, come alive
Dry bones rise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
So I prophesied and there was a rattling sound
Bone came to bone all over the ground
Sinews and flesh and the skin on top
But no breath in them yet, so the story didn't stop
Prophesy to the breath, come from the four winds
Breathe on the slain, let them live again
And the breath came in and they stood on their feet
A vast great army, the valley complete
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
